    <string name="l3_glossary">29. Mini glossary</string>
    <string name="glossary_title">Terms</string>
    <string name="term_activity">Activity</string>
    <string name="term_activity_text">An Activity is a single screen of an app. It has a lifecycle: onCreate, onStart, onResume, onPause, onStop, onDestroy. Every Activity must be declared in AndroidManifest.xml.</string>
    <string name="term_intent">Intent</string>
    <string name="term_intent_text">An Intent is a message to the system describing what should be done. An explicit Intent opens a specific screen of the app, an implicit one (for example ACTION_VIEW) asks the system to find a suitable app: a browser, a dialer, maps.</string>
    <string name="term_layout">Layout</string>
    <string name="term_layout_text">A layout is an XML file that describes a screen: which views (TextView, Button, EditText) it contains and how they are arranged. It is loaded into an Activity with setContentView().</string>

